{
  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_006 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653 accuracy, with multiprofile providing the largest single boost (+0.13 over singleprofile) and scvi_n200 clearly superior to both pca_n2000 and scgpt. Image-only models are very weak (~0.21-0.23), raising the question of whether adding image information to the strong RNA signal helps or merely adds noise. This experiment (config_039) tests the most promising multimodal extension: it pairs the best RNA encoder (scvi_n200) with multiprofile + transformer aggregation (the top RNA-only recipe) and the best image encoder (imagenet_vit_l, marginally better than resnet50), using weighted fusion to allow the model to down-weight the weak image channel. This is the best use of experiment 8 because it directly tests whether multimodal fusion can exceed the 0.653 RNA-only ceiling. If it succeeds, the remaining 2 experiments can refine fusion/aggregation; if it fails, we confirm RNA-only is optimal and can spend the last 2 experiments on minor RNA-only tweaks (e.g., config_003 to confirm scvi > pca in multiprofile, or re-testing with different hyperparameters)."
}

